# This example shows the energy window mode 
# (edited by Andrea Frassà, 11/16/26)
#
# Only events which deposit between 640 and 680 keV in the active detector
# volumes are stored (here: around the 662 keV full energy peak of Cs-137).
# Without detector names all detectors which can trigger count (no guard rings,
# no veto-only detectors); add detector names to restrict it, e.g.:
#   StoreEnergyWindow   640  680  GScinti
#
# Events which can no longer end up in the window are aborted early.
# "Triggers 10000" means 10000 STORED events, TS in the sim file counts all simulated ones.
# Remember: energies are true deposits, the detector resolution is applied later
# (revan/mimrec) - make the window ~3 sigma wider than your analysis window.


# Global parameters:
Version               1
Geometry              $(MEGALIB)/resource/examples/geomega/special/Spheric.geo.setup

# Physics list
PhysicsListEM                        LivermorePol

# Output formats
StoreSimulationInfo                  all

# Energy window (keV)
StoreEnergyWindow                    640  680



# Run: 662 keV narrow beam

Run MyWindowRun
MyWindowRun.FileName                      EnergyWindow
MyWindowRun.Triggers                      10000

MyWindowRun.Source MyWindowSource
MyWindowSource.ParticleType               1
MyWindowSource.Beam                       HomogeneousBeam  0 0 90  0 0 -1  0.1
MyWindowSource.Spectrum                   Mono 662.0
MyWindowSource.Flux                       1.0
